# swarm.conf — one repo per line:  session_name | /path/to/repo | TOKEN_VAR_NAME | CHANNEL_ID | GUILD_ID | ACCOUNT
# session_name: short, no spaces (becomes tmux session "swarm-<name>")
# TOKEN_VAR_NAME: name of the env var in tokens.env holding that repo's bot token
# CHANNEL_ID: Discord channel id (snowflake) this swarm is bound to. Find it in
#   Discord with Developer Mode on: right-click the channel → "Copy Channel ID".
# GUILD_ID: Discord guild (server) snowflake. Find it: right-click the SERVER icon
#   (left sidebar) → "Copy Server ID". Used with CHANNEL_ID by the iOS widget to
#   build discord://channels/<guild>/<channel> deep-links per the frozen
#   swarm-status/v1 contract. Optional during transition (blank → emits null,
#   widget falls back to opening the app); populate it as soon as you know it.
# ACCOUNT (optional, 6th field): multi-account partition label. BLANK = the
#   default account (keychain auth at ~/.claude) = today's behavior — omit it
#   and nothing changes. A <label> pins the swarm to its own config dir
#   ~/.claude-accounts/<label> + the vault token OAUTH_TOKEN_<LABEL_UPPER>.
#   Many swarms MAY share one label (a group sharing one plan's window).
#   Provisioning accounts + tokens is a terms-cleared operator step; the field
#   is inert until accounts exist.
#
#   Examples (6th field = ACCOUNT; blank = default account, beacon+ledger share 'max-a'):
# acme     | /Users/you/code/acme        | BOT_ACME    | 1234567890123456789 | 1111111111111111111 |
# beacon   | /Users/you/code/beacon      | BOT_BEACON  | 2345678901234567890 | 1111111111111111111 | max-a
# ledger   | /Users/you/code/ledger      | BOT_LEDGER  | 3456789012345678901 | 2222222222222222222 | max-a
#
# Keep this list short to start — one or two repos. A single Max pool won't feed
# more than ~1–2 teams running concurrently.
